@startuml P210_issue_vc_proxy_simple

'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
' Settings
'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
'=== Header and Footer ===
header OPEN-DID Technical Specification
footer
  	Page %page% of %lastpage% at %date("yyyy-MM-dd hh:mm:ss")
end footer

'=== Title ===
title
	<size:25>P210 : Issue VC (Proxy Mode)</size>
end title

'=== Options ===
autonumber "<b>(#)</b>"

'=== Participants ===
<style>
participant {
  Padding 20
}
</style>
skinparam BoxPadding 20
skinparam MaxMessageSize 500
skinparam MinClassWidth 80


actor USER

box Mobile #OldLace
    participant "**Wallet**" as WALLET <<Wallet>> #WhiteSmoke
    participant "**CA**" as CA <<App>> #WhiteSmoke
end box

box Certified App Provider #AliceBlue
    participant "**CAS**" as CAS <<WAS>> #WhiteSmoke
    participant "**Proxy**" as PROXY <<Server>> #WhiteSmoke
end box

box TAS Server #AliceBlue
    participant "**TAS**" as TAS <<WAS>> #WhiteSmoke
end box

box Issuer Server #AliceBlue
    participant "**Issuer**" as ISSUER <<WAS>> #WhiteSmoke
end box

box Trusted Storage
    participant "**blockchain**" as BC <<Storage>> #WhiteSmoke
end box


'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
' Content
'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
|||

== Retrieve VC Plan List ==
CA -> TAS++: Request VC Plan List
activate CA
return VC Plan List
CA -> CA: Select a VC Plan whose issuanceMode is PROXY

rnote over CA, CAS
    (Precondition) The CA registers the user information
    verified through KYC or a similar process with the CAS in advance (userId ↔ pii).
end rnote

== P210-1 : Propose Issue VC ==
CA -> PROXY++: Propose Issue VC
    PROXY -> ISSUER++: Inspect Proposal
    return {txId, refId}
return {txId, refId}

== P210-2 : Request Issue Profile ==
CA -> PROXY++: Request Issue Profile {txId, userId}
    PROXY -> ISSUER++: Generate Profile (Proxy) {txId, userId}
        ISSUER -> CAS++: Retrieve PII {userId}
        return {pii}
        ISSUER -> ISSUER: Identify the user to issue to
        ISSUER -> ISSUER: Generate Issue Profile
        opt Include ZKP Credential
            ISSUER -> ISSUER: Generate ZKP Credential Offer
        end
        ISSUER -> ISSUER: authNonce = issuerNonce
    return {txId, profile, authNonce}
return {txId, profile, authNonce}

== P210-3 : Wallet Token Generation ==
rnote across #white
    The process of wallet token generation is not covered in this specification.
    Refer to `issue_wallet_token_simple`
    In proxy mode the ECDH with the TAS and the server token issuance are not performed.
end note

== P210-4 : Request Issue VC ==
CA -> WALLET++: Issue VC request
    WALLET -> WALLET: Generate and sign didAuth {Holder DID, authNonce}
    WALLET -> WALLET: Generate reqVc and encrypt it with E2E
    opt Include ZKP
        WALLET -> WALLET: Generate credentialRequest and include it in reqVc
    end
    WALLET -> PROXY++: Request Issue VC {txId, didAuth, accE2e, encReqVc}
        PROXY -> ISSUER++: Issue VC (Proxy)
            ISSUER <-> BC: Retrieve Holder DID Document
            ISSUER -> ISSUER: Verify didAuth signature and authNonce
            ISSUER -> ISSUER: Decrypt encReqVc and validate it against IssueProfile
            ISSUER -> ISSUER: vc: Issue or Reissue VC
            opt In Case of VC reissuance
                ISSUER -> BC: Revoke existing VC
            end
            opt Include ZKP
                ISSUER -> ISSUER: credential: Issue ZKP Credential
            end
            ISSUER -> BC: Register VC Meta
            ISSUER -> ISSUER: VC<sub>enc</sub> = credInfo E2E encryption
        return VC<sub>enc</sub> response
    return VC<sub>enc</sub> response
    WALLET -> WALLET: credInfo = VC<sub>enc</sub> E2E decryption
    WALLET -> WALLET: Store VC
return {vcId}

== P210-5 : Confirm Issue VC ==
CA -> PROXY++: Confirm Issue VC {txId, vcId}
    PROXY -> ISSUER++: Complete VC {txId, vcId}
    return {txId}
return {txId}
deactivate CA

@enduml
